    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d756">

                <pb facs="0804" n="794" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg794"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.5151/7–549: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister-Counselor of Embassy in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Clark</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Canton</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-07-05">July 5,
                        1949</date>.<lb/>[Received July 5—4:19 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Cantel 690. Official exchange rates based silver currency introduction follow
                    (Cantel 683, July 3, repeated Nanking 458, Shanghai 395).</p>
                <p>HK<anchor n="21" xml:id="d756-f1"/> $1.00 to S $0.24, US $1.00 to S $1.55,
                        Lb<anchor n="22" xml:id="d756-f2"/> 1.00 to S $3.72, ounce gold S $75.00.
                    Current Government revenue estimated 10–15 million silver dollars monthly versus
                    4 [<hi rendition="#italic">sic</hi>] million expenditures, with deficit expected
                    met by bond issues and increased taxes.</p>
                <p>Sent Department Cantel 690; repeated Nanking 465, Shanghai 400.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Clark</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
